<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Compound interest: amount and interest compounded annually (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} invests Ksh \( {@P0@} \) in a SACCO account that pays \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum <strong>compound interest</strong>, compounded annually.</p>
<p>Give your answers to 2 decimal places.</p>
<p>(a) Find the amount in the account after \( {@T0@} \) years.</p>
<div>Amount \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Find the compound interest earned.</p>
<div>Compound interest \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Each year the amount is multiplied by \( 1 + \dfrac{R}{100} = {@float(1 + R0/100)@} \), so</p>
\[ A = P\left(1 + \frac{R}{100}\right)^T = {@P0@}\left(1 + \frac{ {@R0@} }{100}\right)^{ {@T0@} } = {@P0@} \times ({@float(1 + R0/100)@})^{ {@T0@} } = {@r2(A0)@}. \]
<p><strong>(b)</strong> \( CI = A - P = {@r2(A0)@} - {@P0@} = {@r2(A0 - P0)@} \).</p>
<p>Compare: simple interest over the same time would be only \( \dfrac{ {@P0@} \times {@R0@} \times {@T0@} }{100} = {@P0*R0*T0/100@} \). Compound interest is larger because each year's interest also earns interest.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
